message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Turing Decay: A Three-Factor Model of Human Detection of AI-Generated Content, with Preregistered Predictions for Audio and Video"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bussing
    given-names: Jonathan
    affiliation: Independent researcher
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: MIT
keywords:
  - AI-generated content
  - deepfake detection
  - human perception
  - meta-analysis
  - preregistration
abstract: >-
  Pilot re-analysis of 50 face experiments and 17 text results separating
  generator release date from study date. Human detection accuracy falls with
  generator capability within architecture lineages, resets when a new family
  appears, does not improve with background exposure, and rises sharply with
  hands-on expertise. Includes six preregistered predictions for audio and video.
